  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Miracle Bags</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Tiny Miracles Foundation was founded with the objective to send street children to school in Mumbai, India. They soon found out that their impact would be exponentially larger if they could assist the parents to generate an income. This DGGF-TA project has been focused on a collaboration with Rituals Cosmetics, for whom they produced 100,000 cotton bags. This large volume order has led to the creation of 81 direct jobs of which 85% are women. A total of 45 FTE has been indirectly supported with these shipments and 111 people have received trainings on not only stitching, but also with regard to personal skill development, financial skills, human rights and responsibilities. In 2020, Tiny Miracles has been granted Bcorp certification. The first shipment of bags was successful and has now led to new orders, consisting of a total of 1 million bags to be produced in 2021.</narrative>
  </description>
